<description>
Copy the colored neighborhood around the one decorated marker to every matching marker in the lattice.

Input structure
- A square-cell lattice is separated by full horizontal and vertical separator lines.
- Each lattice cell is uniformly colored; most cells are background.
- One marker cell is surrounded by a colored 3x3-neighborhood template, and the same marker color appears elsewhere as isolated cells.

Rule
- Compress the lattice to one value per cell.
- Use the decorated marker's non-background neighbors as relative colored offsets.
- Stamp those offsets around every cell of the marker color, clipping offsets that fall outside the lattice.

Key insight
The separator grid is only scale: the real rule is copying a small colored mask from the exemplar marker to all same-color marker cells.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "colored 3x3-neighborhood mask s around the decorated marker cell",
  "dst": "same-color marker cells d in the block lattice",
  "match_cond": "d.color == decorated marker color",
  "transform": "stamp s's relative colored offsets around each d, clipping at the lattice boundary; preserve separator lines and marker cells"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: square, N*cell_size + (N-1)*1 per side; N=5-10 lattice cells, cell_size=2-4
  lattice:
    separator: single-pixel full-span horizontal and vertical lines of one color (not bg, not any cell color)
    cells: each cell is uniformly one color; background is 0
  template:
    shape: plus (4 cardinal offsets) or full ring (8 surrounding offsets) around center
    center_color: marker_color, distinct from template fill color(s)
    fill_colors: 1-2 non-bg colors; if ring with 2 colors, cardinals get one, diagonals get the other
    symmetry: 4-fold rotational + LR + UD [observed]
    placement: exactly 1 decorated exemplar whose template fits entirely within lattice bounds
  markers:
    count: 2-4 total cells of marker_color (1 decorated + 1-3 isolated)
    isolated: no non-bg 8-neighbor in the cell grid; at least 1 isolated marker present
    no_overlap: stamped template regions across all markers must not conflict
  output: stamp the template offsets around every marker cell (clipping at lattice boundary); separator lines unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick N in [5..10], cell_size in [2..4]. Compute pixel grid = N*cell_size + (N-1).
    2. Choose 3-4 distinct non-zero colors for separator, marker, and 1-2 template fill colors.
    3. Build the NxN abstract cell grid (all bg=0).
    4. Choose template shape (plus or ring) and fill color assignment.
    5. Place the decorated exemplar at an interior position (>=1 cell from each edge) so all template offsets are in-bounds. Write marker + template cells.
    6. Place 1-3 isolated markers at random bg cells ensuring Chebyshev distance >=2 from every non-bg cell and no stamp-stamp overlap (stamps may clip at boundary).
    7. Expand abstract grid to pixel grid with uniform cell fills and separator lines.
```
</generation_spec>
