    placement: mostly isolated singletons; occasional 4-adjacent pairs allowed (2-6 adjacencies total)
  output:
    same as input but all scatter pixels matching marker_color are erased (set to bg)
    the marker pixel at (1,1) is preserved; bracket unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (simple transform, no inversion needed)
  steps:
    1. Create 15x15 bg=0 grid
    2. Place the bracket (color 5) at fixed position - col 3 rows 0-3 and row 3 cols 0-3
    3. Pick marker_color from {1,2,3,4,6,7,8,9} (exclude 0 and 5); place at (1,1)
    4. Choose 7 other distinct colors from {1-9}\{marker_color, 5} plus optionally 5
    5. Scatter 16-32 pixels in the region r>=4 or c>=4, ensuring no cell in bracket bbox
    6. Include 3-5 pixels of marker_color among them (these will be erased in output)
    7. Distribute remaining pixels across other chosen colors (each >=1 instance)
    8. Place pixels mostly isolated; allow a few 4-adjacent pairs but avoid large clusters
    9. Output = copy input, erase all marker_color pixels outside (1,1), restore (1,1)
